lse},"created_at":"2016-10-19T16:03:06Z","updated_at":"2018-11-27T06:02:47Z","body":"**Michael Bayer ([@zzzeek](https://github.com/zzzeek)) wrote:**\n\nSo in particular, this line in the migration notes is wrong: \"If the attribute is not set at all, then column level defaults *will* fire off and/or SQL NULL will be inserted as expected, as was the behavior\npreviously. \" because this is not the previous behavior for a missing default.\n","author_association":"COLLABORATOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/issues/comments/441935052/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"sqlalchemy-bot","id":36047385,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2MDQ3Mzg1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/36047385?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot","html_url":"https://github.com/sqlalchemy-bot","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/issues/comments/441935055","html_url":"https://github.com/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/issues/3830#issuecomment-441935055","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/issues/3830","id":441935055,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDQ0MTkzNTA1NQ==","user":{"login":"sqlalchemy-bot","id":36047385,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2MDQ3Mzg1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/36047385?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot","html_url":"https://github.com/sqlalchemy-bot","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2016-10-19T16:14:09Z","updated_at":"2018-11-27T06:02:47Z","body":"**Michael Bayer ([@zzzeek](https://github.com/zzzeek)) wrote:**\n\nThe ORM has always had the behavior that if a column has no defaults on it, an INSERT will render None for a column's value if it was omitted from the object - the new \"evaulates_none\" flag changes this..   I'm not sure at this point why we need that very old behavior, but it's not coming out in 1.1 at least.  You can make your older behavior work if you do this:\n\n\n```\nclass MyJSON(JSON):\n    should_evaluate_none = False\n\n\nclass Foo(Base):\n    __tablename__ = 'foo'\n    id = Column(Integer, primary_key=True)\n    json = Column(MyJSON(), nullable=False)\n\n```\n\nthis is of course totally non-intuitive so I don't think I'm going to push this as a real workaround.   \n","author_association":"COLLABORATOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/s